  description: Venus is the second planet from the Sun and is similar in size and
    structure to Earth. Its thick atmosphere is composed mainly of carbon dioxide,
    which traps heat and makes Venus the hottest planet in the Solar System.
  interestingFact: Venus rotates in the opposite direction to most planets, meaning
    the Sun would rise in the west and set in the east.
